From: OrientCOMPASS <316423573+OrientCOMPASS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Oct 2026 07:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] btif_av: sink CONNECT_REQ stays passive; PENDING open kept

Now that SEPs correctly advertise TSEP=SNK (0004-avdt), peers act as INT
and push SET_CONFIG to us.  Our stock active BTA_AvOpen on CONNECT_REQ
races ahead of the peer (btsnoop: we SET_CONFIG 2.4 s before the Z40
even opens signalling), marks our SEID in-use, and the peer enters a
DISCOVER->ABORT loop.

Skip the INT open only on the CONNECT_REQ path.  The PENDING path MUST
keep BTA_AvOpen: it feeds bta_av_open_at_inc(), whose native collision
logic parks the request while the peer signals (coll_mask INC_TMR) and
lets the incoming SET_CONFIG win; accept_signalling_timer still falls
back to INT if the peer stays silent.  Dropping the PENDING open left
the lcb/rc half-initialized (bta_av_rc_create "ACP handle exist" spam,
ACL torn down locally, HCI reason 0x16).
---
 btif/src/btif_av.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/btif/src/btif_av.c b/btif/src/btif_av.c
index 2b7adc0..b9ff0d8 100644
--- a/btif/src/btif_av.c
+++ b/btif/src/btif_av.c
@@ -357,8 +357,8 @@ static BOOLEAN btif_av_state_idle_handler(btif_sm_event_t event, void *p_data)
                   }
                   if (bt_av_sink_callbacks != NULL)
                   {
-                      /* passive sink (see CONNECT_REQ_EVT): never INT-open */
-                      APPL_TRACE_DEBUG("btif_av: pending sink - passive ACP mode");
+                      BTA_AvOpen(btif_av_cb.peer_bda.address, btif_av_cb.bta_handle,
+                                 TRUE, BTA_SEC_AUTHENTICATE, UUID_SERVCLASS_AUDIO_SINK);
                   }
              }
              btif_sm_change_state(btif_av_cb.sm_handle, BTIF_AV_STATE_OPENING);
